From 4a15fc7e4636c6fb2e08d5661470003c77dc1fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JerryNee <ni12@illinois.edu>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:36:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Ignore in-source cmake build output

Building with `cmake .` in the source root leaves object directories, a
generated Makefile and static libraries next to the sources, where they are
easy to commit by accident.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 01f9cb9..404443d 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,2 +1,10 @@
 build/
-.vscode/
\ No newline at end of file
+.vscode/
+# in-source cmake build artifacts
+CMakeCache.txt
+CMakeFiles/
+cmake_install.cmake
+cmake_uninstall.cmake
+Makefile
+*.a
+/uxplay
